{"posts":[{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_951","t":"Thank you, DrSwing","a":"angelo20ng","d":"","n":"#951","p":39,"im":[],"m":951},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_952","t":"angelo20ng wrote:\n\nAngelo, do you see any more RBDs or DBR on this chart?","a":"DrSwing","d":"","n":"#952","p":39,"im":["9ca7e5a103bf5ccfef6a04209d8c6509ab1cb760"],"m":952},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_953","t":"DrSwing wrote:\n\nangelo20ng wrote:\n\nYes.","a":"angelo20ng","d":"","n":"#953","p":39,"im":["9ca7e5a103bf5ccfef6a04209d8c6509ab1cb760","578bae1f3b19bd1255dc6c3383e501e15723c461"],"m":953},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_954","t":"","a":"angelo20ng","d":"","n":"#954","p":39,"im":["47580b3534c203e61eaf416039fd51ebcc9a9068"],"m":954},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_955","t":"","a":"angelo20ng","d":"","n":"#955","p":39,"im":["0c8a86ed646de9621238b316ea4553d22b3b68fd"],"m":955},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_956","t":"","a":"angelo20ng","d":"","n":"#956","p":39,"im":["494f86a697727d94954150ba2f389108c884910e"],"m":956},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_957","t":"Hello everyone! I just read caps on price again and I noticed one thing. Please confirm that my assumption is correct.\n\nRBR = Successful bull flag of which top becomes demand. DBD = Successful bear flag of which bottom becomes supply. RBD = Failed bull flag of which bottom (FL) becomes supply. DBR= Failed bear flag of which top (FL) becomes demand.","a":"milkeyway","d":"","n":"#957","p":39,"im":["fd1389ddc3a384f48058300c1373d8bbdba35e94"],"m":957},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_958","t":"Hi Amit, I have attached my understanding.I am curious to know what seniors have to say.This also made me think about the relationship between FTR and RBD/DBR.","a":"harshrthakkar","d":"","n":"#958","p":39,"im":["fc1ab28334871a889f1ea8726c3c374820a33392"],"m":958},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_959","t":"Here I am continuing Home Work again. Caps. If possible, please find my mistakes and guide me. Thanks.","a":"milkeyway","d":"","n":"#959","p":39,"im":["8e800d0a6571fb02dda3945358e764d0e97d611a"],"m":959},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_960","t":"Amit, Its better to get corrected now than to correct later.Ask some senior member to chk the upper two posts correctness.","a":"harshrthakkar","d":"","n":"#960","p":39,"im":[],"m":960},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_961","t":"Hi all I posted some RBD's and DBR's awhile back. I'm back at it again looking for some feedback as to if I'm finding these correctly. It is my understanding that the meaningful RBD's and DBR's move quickly up or quickly. And the bases are rather small and not very wide at all.\n\nAny feedback would be greatly appreciated.\n\nThanks","a":"Ezio","d":"","n":"#961","p":39,"im":["34bd51b70326abed636256fbec6c8c6daeb990ad","13cfe730d43b727165f8a9ff3265d20d8bfacc95","0e18881ac0479d187ab0293fbda169c6d094e6f6","d604e58a124f52e34f8ec7d7aa757170a9915af2"],"m":961},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_962","t":"milkeyway wrote: Here I am continuing Home Work again. Caps. If possible, please find my mistakes and guide me. Thanks.\n\nI made correction to yours Milkeyway.","a":"projectsagana","d":"","n":"#962","p":39,"im":["8e800d0a6571fb02dda3945358e764d0e97d611a"],"m":962},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_963","t":"This is my first homework of DBR/RBD. Not sure if I'm doing it correctly. Please correct me. Thanks!","a":"bulleyes","d":"","n":"#963","p":39,"im":["6f967cb471ac6c76b009eafa99e97e51a3cbc94c"],"m":963},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_964","t":"projectsagana wrote: I made correction to yours Milkeyway.\n\nThanks project. I will take care of it next time.","a":"milkeyway","d":"","n":"#964","p":39,"im":[],"m":964},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_965","t":"Back at it again. Me thinks I'm getting better. Any insight would be appreciated.\n\nThanks in advance","a":"Ezio","d":"","n":"#965","p":39,"im":["f4afcf115fe7ada069a40210e4bdc4e36773339b","6d3e999a29648dec8c1b5148b44d87ac18a55ce1","70b6d5a8a2ca6ac1305af488480c43313e7551d8","d42c3822138067893be690d3752b1674332f4df1"],"m":965},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_966","t":"please criticize. Thanks.","a":"milkeyway","d":"","n":"#966","p":39,"im":["fece3ab788916b4443bf5a02cfe0d02e42517873"],"m":966},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_967","t":"That looks good guys\n\nRemember to attack each exercise with a purpose. Watch how price left each level and how it returned to the level. If a level gets broken, see what price does then and if the level holds where does it go next. It's not just a matter of going through the motions, you have to act like an investigator.","a":"DrSwing","d":"","n":"#967","p":39,"im":[],"m":967},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_968","t":"DrSwing,\n\nThank you very much for the feedback and insight:)","a":"Ezio","d":"","n":"#968","p":39,"im":[],"m":968},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_969","t":"Hi Benhur, i did not understand the concept very well in this post readthemarket.com/index.php/forum/homewo...-drops?start=75#3547. In a RBD the higher price of the box would be where the last buy order filled before the drop, so the High of the candle at the top? And the lower price of the box would be where sellers reversed the PA, then where bullish bar open? Thanks,\n\nGian","a":"gigiocean","d":"","n":"#969","p":39,"im":[],"m":969},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_970","t":"Hi Gian\n\nTo understand how to define a SD zone, we must understand what is behind the zone in terms of Order Flow. We expect that the inner boundary of the zone to be the price where remaining stacks of orders are waiting for execution. Since all we have is the chart, we can spot it by a closer look at the candles. There we look where was the last trade before one side overcome the other. Thinking in Order flow terminology, we may suspect that if one side overcome the other, there might be more orders of the winner side which couldent be filled due to less orders of the loosing side.\n\nUnderstanding this, we can look for this scenario in the chart:\n\nNow, if you understand this, please show me your explained logic of how to mark your zones...","a":"benhur","d":"","n":"#970","p":39,"im":["49d9268fc7f7c94c056a8a04363dbc26a5255ae9"],"m":970},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_971","t":"Is this right?","a":"gigiocean","d":"","n":"#971","p":39,"im":["c4343c317be08f21ddc4b419702fdebf18c709b3"],"m":971},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_972","t":"Your zons are correct. only your logic need a slight adjustment.","a":"benhur","d":"","n":"#972","p":39,"im":["1a10eed1a531f3aa1f58bdb71a1aba5a427f078a"],"m":972},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_973","t":"benhur wrote: Your zons are correct. only your logic need a slight adjustment.","a":"gigiocean","d":"","n":"#973","p":39,"im":["b56d176bcb27a86d9df66e58fce39edf69a270fd"],"m":973},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_974","t":"Zoom in to the same candle, while you think order flow...","a":"benhur","d":"","n":"#974","p":39,"im":["27d378bafd2bf9074dbaaa2c6ec245e2fd929080"],"m":974},{"id":"dbrrbd_p39_975","t":"Unfortunately, the concept fails to enter my head. I still don't undestand where is the last contract.\n\nbenhur wrote: Zoom in to the same candle, while you think order flow...\n\n343536373839404142","a":"gigiocean","d":"","n":"#975","p":39,"im":["27d378bafd2bf9074dbaaa2c6ec245e2fd929080"],"m":975}],"images":[{"k":"9ca7e5a103bf5ccfef6a04209d8c6509ab1cb760","t":"assets/thumbs/9ca7e5a103bf5ccfef6a04209d8c6509ab1cb760.webp","f":"assets/images/9ca7e5a103bf5ccfef6a04209d8c6509ab1cb760.png","w":800,"h":600,"b":20137,"o":"9ca7e5a103bf5ccfef6a04209d8c6509ab1cb760.png","p":39,"pid":"dbrrbd_p39_953"},{"k":"578bae1f3b19bd1255dc6c3383e501e15723c461","t":"assets/thumbs/578bae1f3b19bd1255dc6c3383e501e15723c461.webp","f":"assets/images/578bae1f3b19bd1255dc6c3383e501e15723c461.png","w":800,"h":600,"b":20842,"o":"578bae1f3b19bd1255dc6c3383e501e15723c461.png","p":39,"pid":"dbrrbd_p39_953"},{"k":"47580b3534c203e61eaf416039fd51ebcc9a9068","t":"assets/thumbs/47580b3534c203e61eaf416039fd51ebcc9a9068.webp","f":"assets/images/47580b3534c203e61eaf416039fd51ebcc9a9068.png","w":1188,"h":494,"b":21693,"o":"47580b3534c203e61eaf416039fd51ebcc9a9068.png","p":39,"pid":"dbrrbd_p39_954"},{"k":"0c8a86ed646de9621238b316ea4553d22b3b68fd","t":"assets/thumbs/0c8a86ed646de9621238b316ea4553d22b3b68fd.webp","f":"assets/images/0c8a86ed646de9621238b316ea4553d22b3b68fd.png","w":1188,"h":4